``` ===================================================================================== ```
``` Splunk source tests ```
``` ===================================================================================== ```
``` Run each search separately in Splunk Search & Reporting. Export results as CSV and save ```
``` them as output\splunk\<test id>.csv beside these scripts. ```
```  ```
``` Placeholders to replace once S1 shows your real index and sourcetype names: ```
```   <FW_INDEX>     firewall traffic logs        <DNS_INDEX>   DNS query logs ```
```   <WIN_INDEX>    Windows event logs (DCs)     <ZS_INDEX>    Zscaler NSS / LSS logs ```
```   <FW_ST>, <DNS_ST>, <ZIA_WEB_ST>, <ZPA_ST>     the matching sourcetypes ```
```  ```
``` Field names (src, dest, dest_port, bytes, query, user...) follow the Splunk CIM, which ```
``` most vendor add-ons map to. S3 shows the real field names; adjust the later searches to ```
``` match before running them. ```
```  ```
``` The pilot office filter uses cidrmatch(). Paste the clause from ```
``` output\netbox\pilot_spl_cidr.txt (it uses "src"; copy it and change src to dest where ```
``` a search needs the destination side). ```
```  ```
``` Optional, for all offices at once: upload output\netbox\site_prefixes.csv as a lookup ```
``` file, create a lookup definition "site_prefixes" with Advanced options > Match type ```
``` CIDR(prefix), then use: | lookup site_prefixes prefix AS src OUTPUT site_slug AS src_site ```
``` ===================================================================================== ```


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S1  Index and sourcetype inventory with earliest and latest event. Time range: All time. ```
```     tstats reads index metadata only, so this is fast even over all time. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| tstats count min(_time) as earliest max(_time) as latest where index=* by index sourcetype
| eval days_held = round((latest - earliest) / 86400, 0)
| convert ctime(earliest) ctime(latest)
| sort index sourcetype


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S2  Configured retention per index. Needs permission to run | rest; on Splunk Cloud this ```
```     may be refused, in which case use days_held from S1 and ask the Splunk admin. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| rest /services/data/indexes count=0
| eval retention_days = round(frozenTimePeriodInSecs / 86400, 0)
| table title retention_days maxTotalDataSizeMB currentDBSizeMB totalEventCount minTime maxTime
| sort title


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S3  Field discovery for one sourcetype. Run once per candidate source (firewall, DNS, ```
```     Windows Security, Zscaler). Shows which fields exist and how often they're filled. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<FW_INDEX> sourcetype=<FW_ST> earliest=-24h
| head 10000
| fieldsummary maxvals=5
| eval populated_pct = round(100 * count / 10000, 1)
| table field populated_pct distinct_count values
| sort - populated_pct


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S4  Firewall coverage of the pilot office: which pilot source IPs appear in the last 7 ```
```     days, and whether bytes are recorded. Few or no rows means traffic inside the office ```
```     doesn't cross a firewall that logs to Splunk. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<FW_INDEX> sourcetype=<FW_ST> earliest=-7d
| where (cidrmatch("10.20.0.0/16", src))
| stats count as events sum(bytes) as bytes dc(dest) as destinations by src
| eval has_bytes = if(isnull(bytes), "no", "yes")
| sort - events


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S5  Pilot office flows (both directions), summarised by source, destination and port. ```
```     Feeds the Dependencies tab. Map dest to an office with the site_prefixes lookup. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<FW_INDEX> sourcetype=<FW_ST> earliest=-7d
| where (cidrmatch("10.20.0.0/16", src)) OR (cidrmatch("10.20.0.0/16", dest))
| stats count as events sum(bytes) as bytes by src dest dest_port transport action
| eval gb = round(bytes / 1073741824, 3)
| sort - events
| head 5000


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S6  Long-window check for one server: daily events over the full retention. Shows ```
```     whether monthly, quarterly and year-end activity is visible. Replace the IP; TERM() ```
```     keeps the search fast. Time range: All time (or the retention from S1). ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<FW_INDEX> sourcetype=<FW_ST> TERM(10.20.4.77)
| timechart span=1d count


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S7  DNS query logs: is there a source, does it record the client IP, query and answer, ```
```     and does it cover the pilot office? ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| tstats count min(_time) as earliest max(_time) as latest where index=* (sourcetype=*dns* OR source=*dns*) by index sourcetype
| convert ctime(earliest) ctime(latest)

index=<DNS_INDEX> sourcetype=<DNS_ST> earliest=-24h
| where (cidrmatch("10.20.0.0/16", src))
| stats count dc(query) as distinct_queries values(record_type) as record_types by src
| sort - count


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S8  Domain controller security events: is each DC forwarding, and which authentication ```
```     packages and logon types appear? Field names differ between the classic and XML ```
```     Windows add-ons; S3 on this sourcetype shows which you have. ```
```     4624 logon, 4768/4769 Kerberos, 4776 NTLM credential validation. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<WIN_INDEX> (source="*WinEventLog:Security" OR source="*XmlWinEventLog:Security") EventCode IN (4624, 4768, 4769, 4776) earliest=-24h
| eval auth_package = coalesce(Authentication_Package, AuthenticationPackageName, Package_Name)
| eval logon_type = coalesce(Logon_Type, LogonType)
| stats count by host EventCode auth_package logon_type
| sort host EventCode


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S9  LDAP signing events from domain controllers. 2887 is a daily summary of unsigned and ```
```     cleartext binds; 2889 lists each client, but only when LDAP Interface Events ```
```     diagnostic logging is set to 2 on the DC. Either needs the Directory Service log ```
```     forwarded to Splunk. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<WIN_INDEX> source="*Directory Service*" (EventCode=2887 OR EventCode=2889) earliest=-30d
| stats count latest(_time) as latest by host EventCode
| convert ctime(latest)


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S10 Zscaler logs in Splunk (ZIA NSS and ZPA LSS feeds): which sourcetypes, how far back. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| tstats count min(_time) as earliest max(_time) as latest where index=* (sourcetype=*zscaler* OR sourcetype=*zia* OR sourcetype=*zpa*) by index sourcetype
| eval days_held = round((latest - earliest) / 86400, 0)
| convert ctime(earliest) ctime(latest)


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S11 ZIA web logs: users, apps and volume per ZIA location (office), last 7 days. ```
```     Run S3 on <ZIA_WEB_ST> first: NSS feed fields are set per feed, so names vary ```
```     (for example location, user or login, appname, appclass, reqsize/respsize). ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<ZS_INDEX> sourcetype=<ZIA_WEB_ST> earliest=-7d
| stats dc(user) as users dc(appname) as apps count as transactions by location
| sort - transactions

index=<ZS_INDEX> sourcetype=<ZIA_WEB_ST> earliest=-7d location="<pilot ZIA location>"
| stats dc(user) as users count as transactions by appname appclass
| sort - users
| head 200


``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` S12 ZPA user activity logs: applications reached, by user count, last 7 days. ```
```     Field names depend on the LSS log template; run S3 on <ZPA_ST> first. ```
``` ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
index=<ZS_INDEX> sourcetype=<ZPA_ST> earliest=-7d
| stats dc(Username) as users count as sessions by Application AppGroup
| sort - users
